    "description": "Millennium Parking Garages operates the underground downtown Chicago parking concession beneath Millennium, Grant, and Maggie Daley Parks. Its end users are commuters, residents, tourists, and event visitors, while revenues are derived from parking fees under a long-term concession framework. The asset follows an asset-heavy transportation model based on four underground garages, traffic management systems, and customer access infrastructure. Public sources describe 9,176 parking spaces across 3.8 million square feet, making it the largest underground parking system in the United States. Northleaf and AMP Capital acquired the concession assets in 2016 through Millennium Parking Garages, LLC, and Northleaf continues to list the investment as active.",
